","The mass mass massΔS(II) = Σ nS(product) - Σ nS(reactant)

Given the reaction:
\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} + 3 \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2 \text{POs(s)} + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) \]

With the molar entropics:
\[ S(Pbr) = 91.2 \text{ J/K.mol} \]
\[ S(O_2) = 205.1 \text{ J/K.mol} \]
\[ S(POs) = 66.5 \text{ J/K.mol} \]
\[ S(SO_2) = 248.2 \text J/K.model} \]

The delta S for the reaction is calculated as:
\[ \Delta S = 2 \times S(POs) + 2 \times S(SO_2) - (2 \times S(Pbr) + 3 \times S(O_2)) \]
\[ \Delta S = 2 \times 66.5 \text{J/K.mol} + 2 \times 248.2 \text{J/K.model} - (2 \times 91.2 \text{J/K.model} + 3 \times 205.1 \text{J/K.model}) \]
