   - The number of excess H+ in the final solution is equal to the number of excess H+ in the sum of the two solutions.
   - The number of H+ in the final solution is:
     \[
     N_f \times V_f = 3.00 \, \text{M} \times 20.0 \, \text{L} = 60 \, \text{MM</sub>
     \]
