   \[
   \begin{bmatrix}
   1 & k & 3 \\
   1 & k & -2 \\
   2 & 4 & -3
   \end{pmatrix}
   \begin{bmatrix}
   x \\
   y \\
   z
   \end{pmatrix}
   = \begin{pmatrix}
   0 \\
   0 \\
   0
   \end{pmatrix}
   \]
   For the system to have a non-trivial solution, the determinant of the coefficient matrix must be zero.

2. **Calculate the determinant**:
   \[
   \begin{vmatrix}
   1 & k & 3 \\
   1 & k & -2 \\
   2 & 4 & -3
   \end{bmatrix} = 
   1 \begin{vmatrix} k & -2 \\ 4 & -3 \end{vmatrix} - k \begin{vmatrix} 1 & -2 \\ 2 & -3 \end{vmatrix} + 3 \begin{vmatrix} 1 & k \\ 2 & 4 \end{vmatrix}
   \]
   \[ = 1(-3k + 8) - k(-3 + 4) + 3(4 - 2k) \]
   \[ = -3k + 8 - k + 12 - 6k \]
   \[ = -10k + 20 \]

3. **Set the determinant to zero**:
   \[
   -10k + 20 = 0 \implies 10k = 20 \implies k = 2
   \]

4. **Substitute \( k = 2 \)** into the system of equations:
   \[
   \begin{align*}
   x + 2y + 3z &= 0 \\
   x + 2y - 2z &= 0 \\
   2x + 4y - 3z &= 0
   \end{array}
   \]

5. **Solve the system**:
